# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ROS2 / colcon workspace artifacts
build/
install/
log/
.colcon/
COLCON_IGNORE

# Per-package build artifacts (in case build/ at root gets overridden by negation)
src/*/build/
src/*/install/
src/*/log/

# Generated ROS2 interface bindings (auto-regenerated by rosidl)
src/*/msg/_*.py
src/*/srv/_*.py
src/*/action/_*.py

# Large visualisation meshes (>50 MB). Obtained externally via
# `scripts/download_meshes.sh`; not tracked in git to keep the
# clone size manageable. See src/cobraflex/meshes/README.md.
src/cobraflex/meshes/rplidar-a2m4-r1.stl

# Experimental data — large logs are not version-controlled,
# only their summary CSVs and aggregated tables.
experiments/sim/run_*/raw_logs/
experiments/physical/run_*/raw_logs/
*.bag
*.mcap

# Policy checkpoints — large binary files
policy/checkpoints/*.zip
policy/checkpoints/*.pt
policy/checkpoints/*.pth
policy/checkpoints/*.pkl

# SB3 training artifacts anywhere (checkpoints + replay/vecnormalize) — these are
# large binaries (replay buffers reach several GB, > GitHub's 100 MB limit) and are
# regenerable; only policy/checkpoints/ was covered before, so root-level and
# experiments/ checkpoints leaked into a commit (fixed 25.07.2026).
*.replay_buffer.pkl
*.vecnormalize.pkl
/cobraflex_*.zip
# The 25.07 rule above only caught the `cobraflex_*` naming. SB3's
# CheckpointCallback writes `<run_name>_<steps>_steps.zip`, so a checkpoint
# staged at the repo root for a deploy — e.g. the Phase-5
# `ppo_gz2d_cap022_1M_2024_550000_steps.zip` (20 MB) — was still trackable.
/*_steps.zip
experiments/**/*.zip

# Demo/evidence videos (large; the manuscript references them as supplementary
# material and embeds a still frame instead). Keep the .mp4 under manuscript/media/
# or an experiments run dir; a print PDF cannot play video. Stills (.png) are tracked.
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.webm
*.mov
*.avi
!policy/checkpoints/.gitkeep
!policy/checkpoints/checkpoint_registry.csv

# THE DEPLOYED POLICY. Tracked deliberately, against the rule above, because it
# is the artefact that goes on the car: a safety argument whose subject cannot be
# rebuilt from the repository is not reproducible. 20 MB, and it is the only
# checkpoint that gets this treatment — every other one stays out.
#
# ppo_gz2d_sim2real_v2_2024_r2_1650000_steps.zip — the sim-to-real v2 policy
# (D-72). Chosen on transfer and cage-independence, not reward: best deployment-arm
# statistics of its run (r^2 0.440, bias/swing 0.10, right-turn share 62.1 %) and it
# intervenes on 3.0 % of nominal steps against the reward peak's 35.0 %, which
# matters because D-69 named that C-06 coupling a physical-transfer risk (T2).
# Authorised by a D-43 preflight PASS (max centred ey error 20.9 mm vs 50 mm).
#
# Its paired VecNormalize is NOT tracked and is NOT needed on the car: training
# builds it with norm_obs=False, norm_reward=True, so it carries reward statistics
# only. It is required to *resume training*, not to run the policy.
#
# NOT YET AUTHORISED FOR THE TRACK: sim2real_probe has never been run against real
# circuit imagery, because those frames are absent from the simulation host. See
# docs/17 §7.2.
!policy/checkpoints/ppo_gz2d_sim2real_v2_2024_r2_1650000_steps.zip

# Generated figures (regenerable from data)
manuscript/figures/auto/

# Local configuration
.env
local_config.yaml

# Coverage
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/

# Isaac Sim URDF->USD conversion output (build artifact, re-derivable via
# tools/isaac_import_check.py / tools/build_isaac_urdf.py). The flat
# cobraflex_isaac.urdf is tracked; the heavy USD package is not.
# src/cobraflex/urdf/isaac_usd/

# Misc
# Transient backups (e.g. check_traceability writes docs/08_..md.bak while it
# patches the ODD-Spec, then removes it). Ignored so they never show in status.
*.bak
docs/.phases*
docs/.temp_templates/
tools/assets*
# Ad-hoc sim launch logs from manual evidence sessions (tools/*.sh, validation runs)
/*.log
# Campaign driver by-products: the flock guard file and the per-session stdout
# logs. The campaign's evidence is runs/*/ + campaign_report.json, not these.
experiments/**/.campaign.lock
experiments/sim/campaign_*/*.log

# M-6 camera calibration: keep the raw checkerboard views (the evidence chain for
# the measured HFOV) but not the corner-overlay renders, which are regenerable
# by re-running tools/calibrate_camera_hfov.py board-solve.
experiments/calibration/M6_camera_hfov/**/view_*_corners.png

# Physical-platform rosbags: raw 640x360 lane camera is 13.8 MB/s, so a 2-minute
# circuit recording is ~1 GB. Keep them on the car / on backup, not in git. The
# derived measurements live in experiments/calibration/M7_track_perception.md.
experiments/physical/bags/

# Lane-dataset frames: PNG imagery for closing the appearance gap, ~500 MB per
# few sessions. The labels beside them (labels.csv / rejects.csv) ARE tracked —
# they carry every measurement M-7 §3b cites.
experiments/physical/datasets/*/frames/
experiments/calibration/M7_offset_response_frames/

# frame_capture_node event dumps: the +-3 s PNG neighbourhoods around each
# /perception_invalid or /emergency edge. Same rule as the lane datasets above —
# the imagery stays on the car, the CSV beside it (capture_events.csv) IS tracked
# and carries the event index, reason, trigger time and filename of every frame.
# 31.08.2026 committed 962 MB of these before this rule existed (5 runs, 3248
# PNGs); they are untracked from 01.09 forward and remain retrievable from
# commit 7c496ff5. See docs/CHANGELOG.md [31.08.2026].
experiments/physical/runs/*/frames/
